Conduct comprehensive and deep research on the given user request. Break down into deep and focused sub-queries, and investigate each thoroughly.

Leverage available search/codebase/knowledge/documentation tools and other related resources. Generate concrete research findings and actionable proposals grounded in these findings.

There might be one or more deliverable proposal documents, for example (but not limited to),
- there could be just one deliverable proposal document detailing every proposal in that single document, or
- each proposal has its own deliverable proposal document for all its details, and there can be another overview document.

A deliverable proposal document (NOT the overview one) should include:
- executive summary of key findings and recommended approach;
- detailed research findings with source citations;
- individual proposals ranked by estimated benefit (e.g., performance boost, latency/cost reduction, system simplification, robustness, etc.) with analysis of complexity, risk, and feasibility;
- a manifest of the files, articles, modules, sections, etc. it will create or change;
- open questions that really cannot be addressed without further user input.
